                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "07f1fb94-8b46-4ba3-92e1-c65a3a7a77e2",
                        "entry_id": "c5e78abc-af4c-31b5-b180-d59282183925",
                        "tags": [
                            "superlative"
                        ],
                        "form": "most stubbornly"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "33ad5e5d-97aa-3b6b-bc1a-4d7c7f76e285",
                        "entry_id": "c5e78abc-af4c-31b5-b180-d59282183925",
                        "glosses": [
                            "In a stubborn manner."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "4492e249-4bf8-4f0e-aceb-51ab72e99282",
                                "sense_id": "33ad5e5d-97aa-3b6b-bc1a-4d7c7f76e285",
                                "text": "He stubbornly refused to quit trying, even after failing 20 times."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "beec31d8-e35c-4295-b078-81d48e1ef8d3",
                                "sense_id": "33ad5e5d-97aa-3b6b-bc1a-4d7c7f76e285",
                                "text": "It is the outpost which the devil and the flesh most stubbornly maintain against the assaults of grace; and until it be subdued, and its barriers levelled with the very earth, there is more hope of a fool than of the sinner."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ed8eff4d-19f6-407e-a1f9-42cbcd456e91",
                                "sense_id": "33ad5e5d-97aa-3b6b-bc1a-4d7c7f76e285",
                                "text": "The novel he lends his name to is an account of that life, taking more or less the form of a memoir set down in the years immediately after World War II by an old man mentally preparing for death, not quite at home in the twentieth century (and a little proud of it, stubbornly clinging to his eartrumpet), whose significant memories reach back to the early 1890s and beyond."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ad1c2259-6b50-4b96-bb04-26cbfd605a98",
                                "sense_id": "33ad5e5d-97aa-3b6b-bc1a-4d7c7f76e285",
                                "text": "Bradford may have lost on the night but they stubbornly protected a 3-1 first-leg advantage to emulate a feat last achieved by Rochdale in 1962."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
